          "description": "Review the key takeaways: Mars's apparent eastward-westward-eastward loop is caused by Earth overtaking Mars on its inner, faster orbit. The heliocentric model explains this simply, while the geocentric model required complex epicycles. More distant planets like Jupiter and Saturn show smaller loops. Tap Finish to complete the lab."
